        "raw": "<p>At first glance, I was really disappointed with the foil version of Completionist Guise, which did not appear to have alternate art. However, if you look closer, there are two major differences: He&#39;s bagging a different comic book on the front (Justice Comics vs. Prime Wardens), and threre&#39;s a different quote on the back (&quot;These are from an extremely limited print run.&quot; vs. &quot;I&#39;m going to need like a million dollars for these.&quot;). Clever.</p><p>HOWEVER, if you really want to be a competionist, there&#39;s actually a THIRD version of this card in the Complete Hero Variant Collection. This version has him bagging a copy of Freedom Five, and it has probably my favorite quote of the three (&quot;Some of these have minor variations in the covers that make them really valuable!&quot;). As much as I like this third version, I&#39;m not sure if it&#39;s worth opening up that otherwise duplicate set just to pull out a single card.</p><p>If anyone from GTG is lurking, any insight into the decision to put an exclusive version of this card in the non-foil variant collection only?</p>",
